      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So many maps are grossly insecure due to this, and most scripted moderation tools are incapable to deal with something as simple as a display name change.\n\nI get the fear of people making ban lists, but there are already reporting functions for this, it isn't something that need to be solved on the technical side.\n\nIt even hinders the ability for games to keep track of players that leave the instance and rejoin.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "69af0e8c84f2b8b8fd8661b7",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "65fa77b9ab14b46952dc1993",
        "alias": "Immediate Marlin",
        "aliasID": "65fa77b9a63714bcb3e1eab1",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/b30533afe69642b45d701aeeaa862e87.png",
        "created": "2024-03-20T05:44:25.092Z",
        "name": "Invertex",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5df404cc2072644ac4b5e385",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2026-03-09T18:16:44.314Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5eb6045ff9f4665cc1be132a",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If the VRChat team is worried about data-collection concerns from having a unique ID exposed between different worlds, or the creation of ID-based ban lists, there is an alternative solution:\n\nAdd a secondary private ID to all accounts (not exposed to the account owner either), and then the Worlds API can have a function to request \"getWorldUniqueUserID()\".\n\nVRC central server would then respond with an ID that is generated based on that internal hidden private ID, plus the world ID, and a secret global key only VRC knows about.\n\nThis would provide an ID that remains consistent for each user in a per-world context, but would prevent reverse-engineering to expose any cross-world trackable information.\n\nIt would allow save files to be created in a world that can be both secure and still be restored even if a user completely resets their persistent data (or it gets corrupted). Only breaking if a world is deleted and uploads to a new World ID.\n\nThis would also not add any significant load on VRChat's servers, as it would only calculate it if the call is even made, and cache the result to prevent further calls.\n\n-----------------------------------------------\n\nThinking further into the future, this system could be expanded by replacing the \"world ID\" part of the unique ID generation with a \"shared world ID\", allowing a set of worlds to have a secondary \"shared ID\" value if approved to be linked together. This way if some experiences need to be split across multiple worlds, they can still share the same per-world unique ID for the user. \n\n(But that is something that would have to be approved for linking to avoid large networks of linked worlds just to force shared IDs.)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
